        "original_id": "2e521ac1-c0c4-54ad-b9c5-f3542ebf04bc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gian Carlo Menotti, Ferruccio Busoni\n- Works: The Consul, Arlecchino, Turandot\n- Places: Zurich\n- Topics: opera, double bill performance\n\nFacts:\n- In 1916, Ferruccio Busoni completed the music for the opera Arlecchino while living in Zurich.\n- The Consul is an opera in three acts with music and libretto by Gian Carlo Menotti.\n- The Consul was Gian Carlo Menotti's first full-length opera.\n- Turandot is often performed as part of a double bill with Ferruccio Busoni's earlier one-act opera Arlecchino.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
